# Add boxes to the arm's motion planner's collision world. They JOIN the
# world, they do not replace it: the boxes already there (the planner's
# scene, any added before, the robot's own fixed geometry) all stay. Calls
# are anonymous and accumulate; nothing here removes a box. Publishing
# std_msgs/Empty on /reset returns the planner to the world it loaded at
# boot, dropping every added box, from every caller. Replacing the planner's
# scene by any other means (a whole-world push, by anyone) drops them too.
#
# Refused whole, and the world before it stays: a frame that is not the
# planning frame (the planner transforms nothing), a name already in the
# world (reset first to re-add one), a non-unit orientation, a dim that is
# not a number > 0, or more boxes than the planner can hold. Boxes only: send
# a cylinder's or a sphere's bounding box.
string frame_id                 # the planning frame, arm_mount on RAMMP's robots
CollisionBox[] boxes
---
bool success
string message                  # the world it made, or why it was refused
